  "id": "serotonin-syndrome",
  "term": "serotonin syndrome",
  "definition": "Serotonin syndrome is a harmful drug interaction in which too much serotonin activity in the central nervous system causes changes in mental state, automatic body functions, and muscle or movement control. It most often occurs when serotonin reuptake inhibitors are used together with monoamine oxidase inhibitors.",
